# Layout

Single crate `interpx`. Not a Cargo workspace. Do not create empty files ahead of the Issue that needs them. This includes `justfile` recipes, scripts, and skills' steps that describe a flow that does not exist yet.

```
src/            library
tests/          integration tests, tests/alloc.rs, tests/common/
benches/        criterion benches
examples/       runnable examples used by the README
compare/        pyproject.toml, uv.lock, generate_*.py, goldens/*.json,
                perf/ (Python runners and isolated Rust runner packages)
docs/           design.ja.md, roadmap.md, conventions.md, adr/
```

- `compare/` is not a workspace member. Its Rust runner packages use their own `[workspace]` so their dependencies do not reach `interpx`. Only `compare/goldens/` is in the published package (`include` in `Cargo.toml`).
- Unit tests are `#[cfg(test)]` in the module. Integration tests are in `tests/`. Golden JSON lives in `compare/goldens/` only.
- `docs/design.ja.md` holds the full public specification. `docs/roadmap.md` lists work: ID, title, Issue, status. `docs/conventions.md` holds the directory tree and the responsibility of each module; a row that adds a module adds its line there in the same PR.
- Do not add a dependency the design does not name. A new dependency is a design change first (`.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc`). Heavy dependencies (`convx`, `kiddo`, `faer`) stay behind the `scattered` feature.
